// runtime-program-image-fkb-micro-walker.fk -- Layer 9h5 real PIF trace producer.
//
// Layer 9h5 is the first real trace producer after the terminal supplied-
// evidence 9h4 join. It consumes a request-ready program-image envelope plus an
// admitted byte-decoded PIF admission, walks the admitted in-memory PIF table
// with caller-selected fuel, and emits an existing rpiwt trace row plus a
// micro-walk receipt. Its admitted-AST view also evaluates selected immutable
// byte/u32 expressions, refusing target effects and ambient reads. Completed
// zero-argument strings can be published into their own existing program image
// through the byte codec's retained publication/care flow. The restricted walk
// never executes a target function or trusts a process-held initializer value.
//
